# Line endings
#
# All markdown in this repo is already stored in git as LF (verified against the
# v1.1.5 blobs: zero CR bytes in every tracked .md).
#
# core.autocrlf=true converts these to CRLF in the Windows working tree on
# checkout. Pinning eol=lf keeps the working copy byte-identical to what git
# stores and to what the pinned canonical reference resolves to, which matters
# for a repo whose bootstrap rules turn on exact artifact identity.
#
# This changes no stored content and produces no diff.
*.md text eol=lf

# This file governs its own line endings too, so it does not get converted on
# checkout while defining the rule that prevents conversion elsewhere.
.gitattributes text eol=lf

# Remaining tracked text files. Rules are enumerated rather than declared with
# `* text=auto` on purpose: text=auto checks files out with the platform's
# native ending, which is CRLF on Windows. That is the opposite of the intent
# here. The risk being addressed is not a noisy `git status` -- it is raw
# working-tree bytes being packaged into a static artifact that carries CRLF
# with no git context to reconcile against. Only eol=lf prevents that on disk.
.gitignore text eol=lf
LICENSE text eol=lf

# CI runs these `run:` blocks as bash on ubuntu-latest under `set -euo pipefail`.
# A CRLF checkout appends \r to every line and breaks the scripts.
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
